From: Monea Software <build@hdsatelit.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] GStreamer: add the hdsdvb quirk for the board decoder of satellite receivers

On satellite receivers the board decodes the compressed streams written to
/dev/dvb/adapter0/video0 and audio0 by dvbvideosink and dvbaudiosink
(dvbmediasink), the sinks the receiver software uses for its own player.
The quirk ("hdsdvb" in WEBKIT_GST_QUIRKS and WEBKIT_GST_HOLE_PUNCH_QUIRK)
plays the media on them:

- the parsers stand for the decoders in the codec registry (the board
  decodes), playbin gets native-video and native-audio, and the elements
  that would decode video on the processor (VP8, VP9, AV1, Theora, the
  libav and openh264 video decoders) are kept out, together with the
  parsers of the codecs not measured on the board (HEVC, VP9, AV1);
- the decoders belong to the receiver software, which plays the TV channel
  on them: HdsDvbDecoder borrows them on the UNIX socket named by
  HDS_DECODOR ("cere", answer "ok" once the channel is stopped and the web
  process may open the devices), gives them back when the last board sink
  is finalized ("gata") and sends the video rectangle there ("fereastra"),
  since only the receiver moves the video plane. Without the loan no board
  sink is made: the page gets a decoding error and the board is not
  touched;
- three hooks in GStreamerQuirk for sinks of platform decoders: the
  position read from the decoder (get-decoder-time) instead of the
  position query, which these sinks answer with what was written to the
  driver; the seek flags (key unit instead of accurate: the base sink drops
  the key frame before an accurate segment start and the decoder shows
  nothing until the next one); and the completion of a flushing seek
  without ASYNC_DONE, which non-asynchronous sinks never post.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [satellite receiver configuration]

